id: hu-alien-edu-science-specialist
name: "Science Specialist (Alien)"
system: heroes-unlimited
source_book: Revised Heroes Unlimited p.56
category: occ
occ_group: optional
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { choose: 2, categories: ["Communications"], note: "Printed 56: two communication skills." }
    - { choose: 3, categories: ["Science"], note: "Printed 56: three science skills." }
    - { choose: 2, categories: ["Medical"], note: "Printed 56: two medical skills." }
    - { choose: 2, categories: ["Physical"], note: "Printed 56: two physical skills." }
    - { name: "Computer Operation", base: 60, per_level: 5, note: "Printed 56 grants it outright. 60% is this book''s own base, printed 31." }
    - { name: "Sensory Equipment", base: 40, per_level: 5, note: "Printed 56 grants it outright, as ''read sensory equipment''. 40% is this book''s base, printed 36." }
  occ_related_skills: { count: 0 }
  occ_secondary_skills: { count: 5 }
---

## Lore

Rolled 41-60 on the Alien''s own education table, printed 56, STEP FIVE.

**The Alien does not roll on the Educational Level table.** Printed 27 sends every Power Category to that table except Special Training and Physical Training; the Alien goes there too, and then printed 56 prints a five-outcome table of its own that REPLACES it. So this is an occupation in the same slot as the eleven Educational Levels, and the Alien R.C.C. admits these five and nothing else.

Skill bonus: 1D20%, ROLLED, and not applied to secondary skills.

Printed 56: "A skill bonus of 1D20% applies to all skills except secondary." NO BONUS IS STORED, for the reason the Military Specialist gives: it is rolled, and a choice group takes a number. The two named skills above therefore carry this book''s own base with nothing added. See BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F83.

Printed 56 closes the table with a rule that belongs to all five: *"All aliens can be taught THREE additional secondary Earth skills, but only if taught by a friendly human."* That is a thing that happens in play rather than at creation, so it is not in the secondary count above.

The Alien''s S.D.C. base of 20, its appearance, its homeworld environment and its powers all belong to the Alien R.C.C. on printed 55-59, not here. This class is the schooling and nothing else.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-alien-edu-science-specialist');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
